.Dd November 23, 2026
.Dt LSAPPINFO 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm lsappinfo
.Nd show the running applications
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar command Op Ar args
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the applications LaunchServices' session knows, each named by its
ASN
.Pq Dq ASN:0x0-0x Ns Ar serial Ns Dq : .
An application
.Ar app
is given by its ASN, its process ID, its bundle identifier or its name.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm list
Every application and what is known of it (the default).
.It Cm processlist
Their ASNs, in the order they started.
.It Cm visibleProcessList Op Fl includeHidden
The ASNs of the applications shown in the Dock, the front one first;
hidden ones only with
.Fl includeHidden .
.It Cm front
The front application's ASN.
.It Cm info Oo Fl only Ar key Oc ... Ar app
One application; with
.Fl only ,
only the keys given:
.Cm bundleid , pid , name , bundlepath , executablepath , type , version ,
.Cm hidden , asn .
.It Cm find Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value ...
The ASNs of the applications whose
.Cm bundleid , pid , name
or
.Cm type
match.
.It Cm setfront Ar app
Makes the application the front one.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when an application is not found or the session cannot
be reached; 2 for a wrong command.
